  "mechanismSummary": "Stetter (1973–76) used the benzoin catalysts with a Michael acceptor. The Breslow intermediate, formed from benzaldehyde exactly as in the benzoin condensation, adds 1,4 to methyl vinyl ketone: the ring nitrogen pushes, the former aldehyde carbon bonds to the CH₂ end of the enone, and the charge ends up on the enolate oxygen. Et₃NH⁺ protonates the enolate on carbon, and triethylamine takes the OH proton as the C=O re-forms and the thiazolium ylide leaves. Protonation returns the thiazolium salt. The benzoin reaction competes but is reversible; the Stetter product is not, so it accumulates. The product, 1-phenylpentane-1,4-dione, is a 1,4-diketone made by an acyl anion equivalent: umpolung.",
